-- California Business and Professions Code, Chapter 25.1, the Transparency in Frontier
-- Artificial Intelligence Act (SB 53): baseline of the developer's questions about
-- critical safety incident reporting.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in
-- California law has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: a frontier developer (a company), or a developer asking whether it is one.
-- Every input is a fact that developer can state. The rules are in
-- tfaia-definitions.l4, tfaia-reporting.l4 and tfaia-penalty.l4; this module only asks
-- the questions and builds their records.
-- Units: computing power in integer or floating-point operations (10^26 is
-- 100000000000000000000000000); money in US dollars; dates in ISO 8601; the 15-day
-- clock in calendar days, the day of discovery not counted, extended past a last day
-- that is a Saturday, a Sunday or another holiday you list (Code Civ. Proc. §§ 12, 12a,
-- 135; Gov. Code § 6700(a)(1)); the
-- 24-hour clock in hours.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tfaia-domain`
IMPORT `tfaia-definitions`
IMPORT `tfaia-reporting`
IMPORT `tfaia-penalty`

-- Builds the record of the developer and its model. The revenue field is read only by
-- the large-frontier-developer test; a question that does not ask for revenue passes 0.
GIVEN ai IS A BOOLEAN, broad IS A BOOLEAN, general IS A BOOLEAN, adaptable IS A BOOLEAN
      trained IS A BOOLEAN, used IS A NUMBER, most IS A NUMBER, revenue IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `me and my model`
`the developer and model` ai broad general adaptable trained used most revenue MEANS
    `me and my model` WITH
        `the model is an artificial intelligence model`              IS ai
        `the model was trained on a broad data set`                   IS broad
        `the model is designed for generality of output`              IS general
        `the model is adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks` IS adaptable
        `I have trained, or initiated the training of, the model`     IS trained
        `the operations used to train the model so far`               IS used
        `the most operations I have used or intend to use to train any foundation model I have trained or begun to train` IS most
        `the annual gross revenues of me and my affiliates in the preceding calendar year` IS revenue

-- Builds the record of the incident, in the order of its fields.
GIVEN w IS A BOOLEAN, wh IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `what the model did`, mc IS A BOOLEAN
      single IS A BOOLEAN, people IS A NUMBER, dollars IS A NUMBER, public IS A BOOLEAN
      federal IS A BOOLEAN, loss IS A BOOLEAN, lossh IS A BOOLEAN, dec IS A BOOLEAN
      eval IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the incident as I know it`
`the incident` w wh c mc single people dollars public federal loss lossh dec eval risk MEANS
    `the incident as I know it` WITH
        `there was unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model weights` IS w
        `that access, modification, or exfiltration resulted in death or bodily injury` IS wh
        `the model's conduct`                                                    IS c
        `the model materially contributed to the deaths, injuries, or damage`    IS mc
        `the deaths, injuries, or damage arose from a single incident`           IS single
        `the number of people who died or were seriously injured`               IS people
        `the dollars of damage to, or loss of, property`                         IS dollars
        `the harm came from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model` IS public
        `the harm came from lawful activity of the federal government`           IS federal
        `there was a loss of control of the model`                               IS loss
        `the loss of control caused death or bodily injury`                      IS lossh
        `the model used deceptive techniques against me to subvert my controls or monitoring` IS dec
        `that happened in an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior`        IS eval
        `that behavior demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk`      IS risk

GIVEN d IS A DATE, imminent IS A BOOLEAN, declared IS A BOOLEAN, inforce IS A BOOLEAN, contract IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `my reporting position`
`the position` d imminent declared inforce contract MEANS
    `my reporting position` WITH
        `the date I discovered the critical safety incident`                     IS d
        `I have discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury` IS imminent
        `my declaration under section 22757.13(i) is in effect`                  IS declared
        `the chapter is in force and not preempted as applied to me`             IS inforce
        `a contract between a federal government entity and me strictly conflicts with the reporting duty` IS contract

§ `Am I a frontier developer?`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.11(b), (f), (h), (i)
@export Am I a frontier developer under California's Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act (Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.11(h))? Yes if you have trained, or begun to train, a foundation model for which you have used, or intend to use, more than 10^26 operations of computing power.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", § 22757.11(b))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I a frontier developer` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` MEANS
    `I am a frontier developer` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0)

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.11(a), (j)
@export Am I a large frontier developer under California's Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act (Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.11(j))? Yes if you are a frontier developer and you and your affiliates together had annual gross revenues of more than $500,000,000 in the preceding calendar year.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your model an "artificial intelligence model" within § 22757.11(b) (an engineered or machine-based system that infers from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments)?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, including fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and other material modifications you applied?
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train any one foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included).
      `revenues` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the annual gross revenues, in US dollars, of you and your affiliates (anyone controlling, controlled by, or under common control with you) together, in the preceding calendar year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I a large frontier developer` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `revenues` MEANS
    `I am a large frontier developer` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `revenues`)

§ `Is this a critical safety incident? -- only once something has happened`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.11(c), (d) and § 22757.16
@export Is this event a critical safety incident under California's Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act (Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.11(d))? Only an event involving a frontier model (a foundation model trained with more than 10^26 operations) can be one, and it must be one of four kinds.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved an "artificial intelligence model" within § 22757.11(b)?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many operations of computing power have been used to train the model so far, including fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and other material modifications?
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident?
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, tangible or intangible property did it cause? Leave out any loss of value of equity (§ 22757.16).
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against you, its developer, to subvert your controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is this a critical safety incident` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `operations used so far` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` MEANS
    `it is a critical safety incident`
        (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` FALSE `operations used so far` 0 0)
        (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`)

§ `Reporting a critical safety incident -- only once you have discovered one`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(1), (c)(4), (i); Code Civ. Proc. §§ 12, 12a; SB 53 SEC. 5(d), (e)
@export Must I report this incident to California's Office of Emergency Services under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(1), and by when? A frontier developer reports a critical safety incident with one of its frontier models within 15 days of discovering it: calendar days, the day of discovery not counted, extended when the last day is a Saturday, a Sunday or another holiday you list (other holidays are not computed, so the answer is the earliest possible last day).
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved an "artificial intelligence model" within § 22757.11(b)?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you train the model involved, or initiate its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many operations of computing power have been used to train the model involved so far, including fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and other material modifications?
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train any one foundation model you have trained or begun to train (the one involved included).
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident?
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, property did it cause, leaving out any loss of value of equity?
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against you to subvert your controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
      `the day I discovered it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you discover the critical safety incident (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-02)? The chapter does not define "discovering"; the 15 days are counted from the day after this date.
      `other holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which dates, other than Saturdays and Sundays, are holidays under Code Civ. Proc. § 135 or § 12b: the other days Gov. Code § 6700 lists (with § 135's exceptions) and any day the relevant public office is closed (§ 12b)? Saturdays and Sundays are counted without being listed. No other holiday is computed: fixed-date and nth-weekday holidays (1 January, Thanksgiving and the day after, and the rest) are NOT, so a last day that falls on one is wrong unless you list it. With an empty list the answer is the earliest possible last day.
      `federal route declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you declared to the Office of Emergency Services, under § 22757.13(i)(1), your intent to comply through a federal law, regulation or guidance document the Office has designated by regulation, and is that declaration still in effect (not revoked by you, and the designating regulation not revoked)?
      `chapter in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is Chapter 25.1 in force and not preempted by federal law as applied to you? Answer yes unless a court or a federal law has displaced it for you; the encoding does not decide preemption.
      `federal contract conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a contract between a federal government entity and you strictly conflict with the reporting duty (SB 53, SEC. 5(d))? Usually no.
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the Office of Emergency Services`
`must I report this incident to the Office of Emergency Services, and by when` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` `the day I discovered it` `other holidays` `federal route declared` `chapter in force` `federal contract conflict` MEANS
    `my duty to report to the Office`
        (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0)
        (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`)
        (`the position` `the day I discovered it` FALSE `federal route declared` `chapter in force` `federal contract conflict`)
        `other holidays`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(2), (i); SB 53 SEC. 5(d), (e)
@export Must I disclose this incident within 24 hours under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(2)? A frontier developer that discovers that a critical safety incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury must disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved an "artificial intelligence model" within § 22757.11(b)?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you train the model involved, or initiate its training? (The 24-hour duty is not limited to your own models; this matters only to whether you are a frontier developer.)
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many operations of computing power have been used to train the model involved so far, including fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and other material modifications?
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train any one foundation model you have trained or begun to train.
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident?
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, property did it cause, leaving out any loss of value of equity?
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against its developer to subvert the developer's controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
      `the day I discovered it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you discover the critical safety incident (ISO 8601)?
      `imminent risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury? The 24 hours run from that discovery.
      `federal route declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you declared to the Office of Emergency Services, under § 22757.13(i)(1), your intent to comply through a federal law, regulation or guidance document the Office has designated by regulation, and is that declaration still in effect?
      `chapter in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is Chapter 25.1 in force and not preempted by federal law as applied to you? Answer yes unless a court or a federal law has displaced it for you.
      `federal contract conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a contract between a federal government entity and you strictly conflict with this duty (SB 53, SEC. 5(d))? Usually no.
GIVETH A `my duty to disclose within 24 hours`
`must I disclose this incident within 24 hours` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` `the day I discovered it` `imminent risk` `federal route declared` `chapter in force` `federal contract conflict` MEANS
    `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)`
        (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0)
        (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`)
        (`the position` `the day I discovered it` `imminent risk` `federal route declared` `chapter in force` `federal contract conflict`)

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(1); Code Civ. Proc. §§ 12, 12a
@export Did I report my critical safety incident to California's Office of Emergency Services in time under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(1)? The last day is the 15th calendar day after the day of discovery, moved to the next day that is not a holiday if it falls on a Saturday, a Sunday or another holiday you list.
GIVEN `the day I discovered it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you discover the critical safety incident (ISO 8601)?
      `the day I reported it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you report it to the Office of Emergency Services (ISO 8601)?
      `other holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which dates, other than Saturdays and Sundays, are holidays under Code Civ. Proc. § 135 or § 12b: the other days Gov. Code § 6700 lists (with § 135's exceptions) and any day the relevant public office is closed (§ 12b)? Saturdays and Sundays are counted without being listed. No other holiday is computed: fixed-date and nth-weekday holidays (1 January, Thanksgiving and the day after, and the rest) are NOT, so a last day that falls on one is wrong unless you list it. With an empty list the answer is the earliest possible last day.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` `the day I discovered it` `the day I reported it` `other holidays` MEANS
    `I reported to the Office in time` `the day I discovered it` `the day I reported it` `other holidays`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(2)
@export Did I make my imminent-risk disclosure within 24 hours under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(2)? A disclosure exactly 24 hours after you discovered the imminent risk is in time.
GIVEN `hours taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours passed between your discovering that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury and your disclosure to an appropriate authority?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`did I disclose within 24 hours` `hours taken` MEANS
    `I disclosed within 24 hours` `hours taken`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(3)
@export May I file an amended critical safety incident report under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(c)(3)? You may if you discover information about the incident after filing your initial report.
GIVEN `filed initial report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed your initial report of the critical safety incident?
      `new information after filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you discover information about the incident after filing that initial report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may I file an amended report` `filed initial report` `new information after filing` MEANS
    `I may file an amended report` `filed initial report` `new information after filing`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(a)
@export What must my critical safety incident report to California's Office of Emergency Services give, under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(a)? Four items.
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of a critical safety incident report`
`what must my report give` MEANS
    `the items a critical safety incident report gives`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(f)
@export Is my critical safety incident report exempt from the California Public Records Act under Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.13(f)? A report submitted to the Office of Emergency Services under § 22757.13 is.
GIVEN `submitted under 22757.13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit the report to the Office of Emergency Services under § 22757.13?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my report exempt from public records requests` `submitted under 22757.13` MEANS
    `my report is exempt from the California Public Records Act` `submitted under 22757.13`

§ `What can happen to me if I do not report -- only if you failed to report`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.15
@export What is the most I can be made to pay if I fail to report a critical safety incident under California's Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act (Bus. & Prof. Code § 22757.15)? Only a large frontier developer is subject to the civil penalty: up to $1,000,000 per violation, depending on severity, recovered only by the Attorney General.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your model an "artificial intelligence model" within § 22757.11(b)?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, including fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and other material modifications?
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train any one foundation model you have trained or begun to train.
      `revenues` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the annual gross revenues, in US dollars, of you and your affiliates together in the preceding calendar year?
      `the failure` IS A `a failure of mine` @desc What did you fail to do? One of: I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days; I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours.
      `violations` IS A NUMBER @desc How many violations are you counting? The chapter does not say how violations are counted.
      `chapter in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is Chapter 25.1 in force and not preempted by federal law as applied to you? Answer yes unless a court or a federal law has displaced it for you.
